{"id":39,"date":"2010-10-18T21:34:18","date_gmt":"2010-10-18T19:34:18","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/panamriders.biketravellers.com\/?p=39"},"modified":"2010-10-18T21:35:58","modified_gmt":"2010-10-18T19:35:58","slug":"hiker-biker-sites-and-youth-hostels-at-the-usa-westcoast","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"http:\/\/panamriders.biketravellers.com\/hiker-biker-sites-and-youth-hostels-at-the-usa-westcoast\/","title":{"rendered":"Hiker-biker sites and Youth Hostels at the USA Westcoast"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>John Benson has provided the Panam &amp; West-Coast cyclists with a very useful document, with a list of all Hiker-Biker sites, Youth Hostels and more useful info. Thanks John!<\/p>\n<p>&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;<\/p>\n<p>Hi Harry<\/p>\n<p>Here&#8217;s the document, attached.<\/p>\n<div id=\"attachment_42\" style=\"width: 310px\" class=\"wp-caption alignright\"><a href=\"http:\/\/panamriders.biketravellers.com\/files\/2010\/10\/20081205-_MG_1598South_on_the_foggy_Redwood_Highway-_California.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-42\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-42\" title=\"Going South on the USA Westcoast, foggy Oregon\" src=\"http:\/\/panamriders.biketravellers.com\/files\/2010\/10\/20081205-_MG_1598South_on_the_foggy_Redwood_Highway-_California-300x209.jpg\" alt=\"Going South on the USA Westcoast, foggy Oregon\" width=\"300\" height=\"209\" srcset=\"http:\/\/panamriders.biketravellers.com\/files\/2010\/10\/20081205-_MG_1598South_on_the_foggy_Redwood_Highway-_California-300x209.jpg 300w, http:\/\/panamriders.biketravellers.com\/files\/2010\/10\/20081205-_MG_1598South_on_the_foggy_Redwood_Highway-_California-150x104.jpg 150w, http:\/\/panamriders.biketravellers.com\/files\/2010\/10\/20081205-_MG_1598South_on_the_foggy_Redwood_Highway-_California.jpg 1000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a><p id=\"caption-attachment-42\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Going South on the USA Westcoast, foggy Oregon<\/p><\/div>\n<p>It&#8217;s not quite what the title says and you can obviously adapt it as you wish. There are two bits to it:<br \/>\n1. North of San Francisco<br \/>\n2. South of San Francisco<br \/>\nI stayed with friends in SF so didn&#8217;t put options there for the city.<\/p>\n<p>North of San Francisco it&#8217;s easy &#8230; there is only one HI Hostel in Point Reyes so everything else is an H\/B site. Each site has 4 sections:<br \/>\n1. Name of campsite where the H\/B is.<br \/>\n2. Location.<br \/>\n3. Distance from the previous camp &#8211; the first one is from the last site in Oregon, a mile north of Brookings.<br \/>\n4. Any extra notes e.g. the first site closes after Labo(u)r Day &#8211; 6 September.<\/p>\n<p>South of San Francisco has H\/B sites, HI Hostels &amp; W\/showers &#8211; the latter only where I stayed.<br \/>\nThis time there are 5 columns &#8211; the same four as above and a new 4th column which indicates where I stopped each night and the distance I took to get there &#8211; with stops, getting lost etc.<br \/>\nI used a couple of hostels for breaks from camping or in Santa Monica, as a base to see LA, where there aren&#8217;t any campgrounds.<br \/>\nOne important point to note is that North Beach Campground in Pismo Beach is no longer an H\/B site and so there is a long distance between Morro Bay &amp; Gaviota State Park (basically, 2 days cycling for the normal person). It&#8217;s $25 per site at North Beach so, if there are other cyclists, you can share a site or ask around. By Pismo Beach, there were only 4 of us running the route at the same time, unlike at other times, so this may be a limited option.<\/p>\n<p>&#8212;<br \/>\nJohn<br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.johnbensontravels.com\/\" target=\"_blank\">www.johnbensontravels.com<\/a><br \/>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.johnbensontravels.com\/currenttrip.html\" target=\"_blank\">www.johnbensontravels.com\/currenttrip.html<\/a><\/p>\n<p>The document:<